PROMPT 36 — THE LOYALTY TEST
Investigate whether political loyalty to an individual is becoming a meaningful criterion for federal appointment, retention, promotion, or removal.
Do not use isolated rhetoric as proof.
Find institutional evidence.
SEARCH
* personnel announcements
* transition documents
* loyalty questionnaires
* public statements
* hiring criteria
* firing explanations
* reassignment patterns
* inspector-general removals
* prosecutor removals
* military leadership removals
* intelligence leadership changes
* civil-service reclassification
* agency directives
DISTINGUISH
* ordinary policy alignment
* partisan appointment
* ideological compatibility
* presidential loyalty
* personal loyalty
* refusal to obey unlawful orders
* insubordination
* normal management discretion
CASE FILE FORMAT
For each example:
* person
* position
* date
* action
* stated reason
* documentary evidence
* alternative explanation
* legal status
* confidence
OUTPUT
Working title:
The Loyalty Test
Include a section titled:
Policy Loyalty Is Not Personal Loyalty
Make that distinction explicit.

